content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 7.1 mm/s RMS at the drive-end bearing housing. This is above Zone A (0.0-2.8) and Zone B (2.8-4.5), and exactly on the boundary between Zone C (4.5-7.1: restricted; plan maintenance) and Zone D (7.1-11.0: damage likely; stop the pump). Figure 3 expressly does not establish which zone owns an exact boundary value, so the reading cannot definitively be classified as either C or D.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Interim decision: stop P-103 now and treat the reading as a potential highest-severity-zone case pending reliability review. If it is Zone D, SSP-07 requires immediate shutdown and notification of the reliability engineer before restart. P1 is a conservative planning response to that possibility, not a documented vibration-to-priority mapping.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The applicable temperature limits are for bearing-housing surface temperature. At 72 C, the housing is 2 C above the normal limit of 70 C, but remains below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits. Thus the normal limit is exceeded, but neither the alarm nor trip threshold is reached, and SSP-07's temperature-based requirement for a priority-1 work order above the alarm limit is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only the drive-end vibration reading is supplied. The manual requires weekly measurement on both bearing housings and classification/action using the highest reading, so the overall pump classification is incomplete until the other housing is measured under an authorised running plan.",
      "citations": [
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leak is reported. Consequently, the troubleshooting row for leakage at the shaft seal does not provide a basis for automatic mechanical-seal replacement; the applicable symptom rows are high vibration and elevated bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Check bearing wear and misalignment first, without ranking between them: both are documented causes of high vibration and high bearing temperature, making them common explanations for the two abnormal readings. Neither is yet confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented cause of high bearing temperature; check grease quantity before attributing the temperature rise solely to bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage is an alternative documented cause of high vibration and requires impeller inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is another documented cause of high vibration; check NPSH. The report contains no evidence confirming or excluding it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-103 immediately as an interim precaution and prevent restart. Notify the reliability engineer of the exact 7.1 mm/s RMS boundary reading before any restart; do not represent the reading as conclusively Zone C or Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal pump or seal work, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC; mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves; and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-103 is on the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed filtered-water line.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If internal access requires removal of the back pull-out assembly, arrange a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment before lifting: the assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Diagnose before authorising parts replacement: check grease quantity, inspect the bearings and impeller, check NPSH, and check shaft alignment for the reported vibration and elevated housing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If inspection confirms wear, noise or high temperature in either bearing, replace both bearings as a pair. Where M12 bearing-housing bolts are disturbed and refitted, tighten them to 85 Nm on lightly oiled threads. The 72 C reading alone does not establish which bearing defect, if any, is present.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any repair that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not add mechanical-seal replacement to the base scope solely on the current report. If subsequent inspection authorises seal work, follow manual procedure 5.2 and the serial-specific bulletin decision in source_conflicts, including a new casing gasket and the 30 Nm gland torque rather than the obsolete 25 Nm value for this application.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any running diagnostic test or return to service, notify the reliability engineer and resolve the boundary/restart instruction. If running is authorised, measure vibration on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading, and record both results. Maintain Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Potential highest-zone vibration: apply an interim immediate stop and reliability-engineer notification before restart while the exact 7.1 mm/s RMS boundary classification remains unresolved.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Internal pump/seal work: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical exposure: P-103 is within P-101 to P-106 on the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed filtered-water line, so chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required for work on the line.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting: the 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds 25 kg; use a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment whenever that assembly is lifted.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal protection during any authorised running or restart: use Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement: Table 6 allows 6.0 hours with 2 technicians for replacement of the bearing pair; include this only if inspection confirms the bearing-replacement scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser alignment: Table 6 allows 1.5 hours with 1 technician when alignment is performed.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If seal replacement is separately authorised later, the manual's standard allowance is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians; it is not included in the base diagnostic scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal specification/torque conflict: manual procedure 5.2 sends fasteners to Table 5, whose M10 seal-gland torque is 25 Nm. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead prohibits HF3-450 and specifies pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B with 30 Nm gland torque for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-103 is HF3-22410, so the bulletin applies to this asset. If seal work is later authorised, do not fit HF3-450; use HF3-450B at 30 Nm, with no sleeve measurement needed to set the pre-set seal. The manual's other fastener torques are not superseded by this decision.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve disposition for this serial: the manual generally requires inspection for scoring, while the applicable bulletin supplies the specific replacement criterion. If the seal/sleeve area is inspected, replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; do not treat the pre-set seal's elimination of installation sleeve measurement as eliminating the scoring inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does AquaDyne or Westfield assign exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS to Zone C or Zone D, and what restart criterion applies? Figure 3 leaves exact-boundary ownership unresolved (C07). Obtain this decision from the reliability engineer/manufacturer rather than assuming a zone.",
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration velocity? Both housings must be measured and the highest reading classified, but only the drive-end reading is available (C06).",
    "Which root cause is confirmed by grease, bearing, impeller, alignment and NPSH checks? The current readings do not establish whether bearings, alignment or other components require replacement (C09).",
    "No replacement parts are released for the base scope. If bearings, impeller components or a casing gasket are required, their part numbers are not provided. Confirm the supported parts after inspection; do not guess bearing or gasket part numbers (C09, C10).",
    "If seal work is later authorised, what are the observed seal condition and shaft-sleeve scoring depth? HF3-455 is conditional on scoring exceeding 0.1 mm, and no leak is currently reported (C13).",
    "Table 6 provides no standard labour time for shutdown, isolation, lifting, grease/NPSH checks or diagnostic inspection. Those durations and any required additional technicians remain to be planned (C12).",
    "The correct grease quantity/specification, NPSH acceptance data and post-repair vibration acceptance criterion are not included in the evidence; obtain them before closing those checks.",
    "Review the interim P1 priority if the reliability engineer rules out Zone D. SSP-07 explicitly mandates priority 1 for bearing temperature above the 80 C alarm, which 72 C does not meet, but provides no vibration-zone priority mapping (C02, C15)."
  ]
}
